-- check/bad: the other half of the nested-`()` defect. `Just ()` matches
-- every `Just`, because `()` has exactly one value, so the `Just _` below
-- it can never run — the same answer `Just ( a, b )` then `Just _` gives.
-- A relation that could not specialise a nested unit at all would report
-- this branch as useful (checker.md §6).
pub label : Maybe () -> Int
label m =
    case m of
        Just () ->
            1

        Just _ ->
            2

        Nothing ->
            0
